 "title": "Price falls as the yield rises",
 "caption": "The 3-year 5% coupon bond is worth £100 (par) when the yield equals the coupon, 5%. At a 6% yield it is £97.33, below par; a lower yield would put it above par.",
 "alt": "A downward-sloping curve of price against yield, passing through £100 at 5% and £97.33 at 6%.",
 "description": [
  "Price = 5/(1 + y) + 5/(1 + y)² + 105/(1 + y)³.",
  "At y = 5% (the coupon) the price is exactly £100.",
  "At y = 6% it is 4.717 + 4.450 + 88.160 = £97.33.",
  "Higher yields discount the cash flows more, so the price falls."
